.local*
.cache

# PaddleBoard: personal files. Anything in `.private/` stays on your machine, and
# the project ships no Claude config, so `.claude/` is yours too. See
# CONTRIBUTING.md, "Keeping your own files". The Fork guards workflow fails a PR
# that adds either with `git add -f`. No trailing slashes: `.claude` is often a
# symlink, and a pattern ending in `/` matches only a real directory.
/.private
/.claude
